OL,3,GNEWSABeer and wine in Wales costs more
OL,4,Aas minimum alcohol price rises by 30%
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe minimum price of alcohol (MUP) in
OL,7,FWales has risen by 30%, to bring the
OL,8,Frate in line with Scotland.
OL,10,FSome people in Cardiff welcomed the
OL,11,Fchange on Thursday, which means
OL,12,Flow-cost alcohol will now be more
OL,13,Fexpensive to buy, while others feared
OL,14,Fit could impact a hospitality industry
OL,15,Fwhich is "already in a state of
OL,16,Fcrisis".
OL,18,FAlcohol Change UK supported the rise
OL,19,Fand said there would be "little or no
OL,20,Fchange" for moderate drinkers, as the
OL,21,Fpolicy would not change the price of a
OL,22,Fpint.
OL,23,APub: 01-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
